NavigationItemSchema currently treats all type-specific target fields (objectName/dashboardName/pageName/reportName/url) as optional regardless of `type`, so invalid items like `{type:'object', label:'x'}` will pass schema validation. Consider using `z.discriminatedUnion('type', ...)` (or a `.superRefine`) to require the correct field(s) per type (and to require `children` for `group`, forbid incompatible fields for `separator`, etc.).
```suggestion
export const NavigationItemSchema: z.ZodType<any> = z.lazy(() => {
  /**
   * Base fields shared by all navigation item types.
   */
  const BaseNavigationItemSchema = z.object({
    id: z.string().describe('Unique identifier'),
    label: z.string().describe('Display label'),
    icon: z.string().optional().describe('Icon name (Lucide)'),

    // Visibility & Permissions
    visible: z.union([z.boolean(), z.string()]).optional().describe('Visibility expression'),
    requiredPermissions: z.array(z.string()).optional().describe('Required permissions'),

    // UX Enhancements
    badge: z.union([z.string(), z.number()]).optional().describe('Badge text or count'),
    badgeVariant: z.enum(['default', 'destructive', 'outline']).optional().describe('Badge variant'),
    defaultOpen: z.boolean().optional().describe('Group default expanded state'),
    pinned: z.boolean().optional().describe('Pinned item'),
    order: z.number().optional().describe('Sort order weight'),
  });

  const ObjectNavigationItemSchema = BaseNavigationItemSchema.extend({
    type: z.literal('object').describe('Navigation item type'),

    // Type-specific target fields
    objectName: z.string().describe('Target object name (type: object)'),
  });

  const DashboardNavigationItemSchema = BaseNavigationItemSchema.extend({
    type: z.literal('dashboard').describe('Navigation item type'),

    // Type-specific target fields
    dashboardName: z.string().describe('Target dashboard name (type: dashboard)'),
  });

  const PageNavigationItemSchema = BaseNavigationItemSchema.extend({
    type: z.literal('page').describe('Navigation item type'),

    // Type-specific target fields
    pageName: z.string().describe('Target page name (type: page)'),
  });

  const ReportNavigationItemSchema = BaseNavigationItemSchema.extend({
    type: z.literal('report').describe('Navigation item type'),

    // Type-specific target fields
    reportName: z.string().describe('Target report name (type: report)'),
  });

  const UrlNavigationItemSchema = BaseNavigationItemSchema.extend({
    type: z.literal('url').describe('Navigation item type'),

    // Type-specific target fields
    url: z.string().describe('Target URL (type: url)'),
    target: z.enum(['_blank', '_self']).optional().describe('Link target (type: url)'),
  });

  const GroupNavigationItemSchema = BaseNavigationItemSchema.extend({
    type: z.literal('group').describe('Navigation item type'),

    // Grouping
    children: z
      .array(z.lazy(() => NavigationItemSchema))
      .min(1)
      .describe('Child items (type: group)'),
  });

  const SeparatorNavigationItemSchema = BaseNavigationItemSchema.extend({
    type: z.literal('separator').describe('Navigation item type'),
  });

  const ActionNavigationItemSchema = BaseNavigationItemSchema.extend({
    type: z.literal('action').describe('Navigation item type'),
  });

  return z.discriminatedUnion('type', [
    ObjectNavigationItemSchema,
    DashboardNavigationItemSchema,
    PageNavigationItemSchema,
    ReportNavigationItemSchema,
    UrlNavigationItemSchema,
    GroupNavigationItemSchema,
    SeparatorNavigationItemSchema,
    ActionNavigationItemSchema,
  ]);
});
```

The transform maps `MenuItem.path` directly to `pageName` (and the tests assert values like "/dashboard"), but console routing and PageView look up pages by name (e.g. "help" / "crm_help"), not route paths with leading slashes. This will produce broken URLs like `/apps/:app/page//dashboard` and fail page lookups. Strip leading slashes and/or extract the last path segment when mapping `path` → `pageName`, and update the mapping comment accordingly.
```suggestion
  // Path-based item → treat as page navigation; derive pageName from last path segment (no leading slash)
  const rawPath = item.path || '';
  const pageName =
    rawPath
      .split('/')
      .filter(Boolean)
      .pop() || '';

  return {
    id,
    type: 'page',
    label: item.label || '',
    icon: item.icon,
    pageName,
```

Area switching currently ignores `NavigationArea.visible` and `NavigationArea.requiredPermissions`, so areas intended to be hidden (expression/RBAC) will still be shown and selectable. Filter `areas` using `evaluateVisibility(area.visible, evaluator)` and the same permissions check used for nav items, and ensure the default `activeAreaId` selects the first *visible/allowed* area.
```suggestion
  const { evaluator } = useExpressionContext();
  const visibleAreas = React.useMemo(
    () =>
      areas.filter((area: any) =>
        evaluateVisibility(area?.visible, evaluator),
      ),
    [areas, evaluator],
  );
  const [activeAreaId, setActiveAreaId] = React.useState<string | null>(
    () => (visibleAreas.length > 0 ? visibleAreas[0].id : null),
  );

  // Reset area when app changes or areas become available
  React.useEffect(() => {
    if (visibleAreas.length > 0) {
      setActiveAreaId(prev =>
        visibleAreas.some((a: any) => a.id === prev) ? prev : visibleAreas[0].id,
      );
    } else {
      setActiveAreaId(null);
    }
  }, [activeAppName, visibleAreas.length]);

  // Resolve navigation items: area navigation > flat navigation > empty
  const activeArea = visibleAreas.find((a: any) => a.id === activeAreaId) ?? null;
```

The `useEffect` that resets `activeAreaId` only depends on `areas.length`, so changes to the area list (IDs/order/visibility) that keep the same length won't update selection. Consider depending on a stable derived key (e.g. `areas.map(a => a.id).join(',')`) or the `areas` reference itself to keep `activeAreaId` in sync with metadata updates.
```suggestion
  }, [activeAppName, areas]);
```
